"""Leading with AI (Leadership Edition), Session 1: AI that sees and reads: images, documents and speech.  Written 12 November 2026.

The pattern of the pilots (Sessions 0 and 2): a bridge from Session 0 and a hook with a real case; the idea as a ladder of pictures with no
maths; the six-industry tour and three case stories; a recorded demonstration plus one clearly marked live demonstration with a fallback;
your people; questions to ask; the portfolio hands-on; the decision; the take-away.  It teaches exactly what Session 2's recall asks:
how a model learned to tell a diseased leaf from a healthy one (labelled photos), that reading documents and speech-to-text are the same
idea, and when a picture model struggles (a new picture that differs from its examples).

Cases (research/*.md): AGR-02 Makerere cassava app (hook, and the "undetermined" lesson), HLT-09 Google Health in Thai clinics (struggle),
AGR-01 PlantVillage Nuru (one-line recall of Session 0), tour tiles TEL-09 Orange, GAP-21 Farmers Companion App, MFG-04 Coca-Cola HBC,
HLT-04 Makerere AI Health Lab, GAP-08 Judiciary of Uganda; case stories AGR-07 One Acre Fund Burundi, HLT-10 MASAI trial, PUB-04
Judiciary of Kenya; RTL-07 Uber Eats (your people: appeal).  Not used from the plan list: ENR-04 Rio Tinto (machines that act belong to
Session 10).  No banking case reads images or documents in the case bank, so the banking tile says so.
Demonstration: the recorded digit network in demo_runs/s01/ (digits_run.py; scikit-learn 1.9.1; 5 November 2026; one main run,
deterministic, run twice with identical output, plus five random starts).  The receipt reading is LIVE with a fallback; no recorded run of it
exists and none is claimed.  Leaves, forms, sound pictures and the Nile Valley Foods entry are illustrations; Nile Valley Foods is fictional.
"""

